  15:     """
  16:     Drop every large foreground object straight down to the bottom while leaving small marker objects fixed.
  17: 
  18:     Input structure:
  19:     - The grid has a dominant background color and exactly one foreground color.
  20:     - The foreground is split into separated 4-connected objects.
  21:     - Objects of area at most three are stationary markers; larger objects are moving sprites.
  22: 
  23:     Rule:
  24:     - Clear each moving sprite from its original position.
  25:     - Translate each moving sprite vertically downward until its bbox bottom reaches the grid bottom.
  26:     - Repaint each translated sprite in its original color; small markers stay unchanged.
  27: 
  28:     Key insight:
  29:     - Object area separates the active falling sprites from the small fixed markers, and all active sprites follow the same vertical path.
  30:     """
